1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:06,131
D-Did... I'm sorry

2
00:00:06,173 --> 00:00:08,884
did you just say
it's Rachel?

3
00:00:09,927 --> 00:00:12,095
Yes.

4
00:00:13,764 --> 00:00:16,892
Um, you-you
like Rachel?

5
00:00:18,435 --> 00:00:22,063
Yes. I like Rachel.

6
00:00:28,946 --> 00:00:30,572
Rachel?!

7
00:00:30,614 --> 00:00:31,991
Yeah, okay

8
00:00:32,031 --> 00:00:33,450
( stammering )

9
00:00:33,492 --> 00:00:35,911
Hey, you know... you
know who else I like?

10
00:00:35,953 --> 00:00:38,413
You. And-and it doesn't
get said enough.

11
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:40,916
I like you, Ross.

12
00:00:41,959 --> 00:00:43,836
R-R-Rachel Rachel?

13
00:00:43,878 --> 00:00:45,212
Yeah. It's not a big deal.

14
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:46,588
It's not a big deal?

15
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:48,340
Oh, I'm sorry. I just...

16
00:00:48,382 --> 00:00:51,969
Um, I... What about all
the stuff you-you just said?

17
00:00:52,011 --> 00:00:53,220
I mean, how about, uh, like

18
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:54,805
you can't stop thinking
about her.

19
00:00:54,847 --> 00:00:57,224
Like, how you can't sleep.

20
00:00:57,265 --> 00:00:59,601
I-I'm an actor, you know.

21
00:00:59,643 --> 00:01:03,397
As-As a group we tend
to be overdramatic.

22
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:06,901
But Rachel-who's-carrying-
my-baby Rachel?

23
00:01:06,942 --> 00:01:09,987
Look, no, I-I know it's bad
and I know it's wrong, okay?

24
00:01:10,029 --> 00:01:13,574
But-But it's not like anything's
ever going to happen, you know.

25
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:15,283
These-These are just feelings.

26
00:01:15,325 --> 00:01:17,036
They-They're going to go away.

27
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:19,079
You know, I-I got to go.

28
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:20,163
Aw, come on, Ross.

29
00:01:20,205 --> 00:01:21,289
Hey, Ross, Ross...
I don't...

30
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:22,290
I just... you know

31
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:25,002
I-I just have one...
Rachel?!

32
00:01:27,046 --> 00:01:28,380
( sighs )

33
00:01:29,464 --> 00:01:31,466
( no audio )

34
00:01:35,971 --> 00:01:36,931
( sighs )

35
00:01:36,972 --> 00:01:38,139
Rachel?!

36
00:01:47,066 --> 00:01:51,278
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

37
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:53,530
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

38
00:01:53,572 --> 00:01:55,657
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

39
00:01:55,699 --> 00:02:00,495
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

40
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:02,790
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

41
00:02:02,831 --> 00:02:06,085
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

42
00:02:06,125 --> 00:02:09,337
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

43
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:15,385
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

44
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:20,432
Yeah. Oh, oh!

45
00:02:20,474 --> 00:02:22,350
Okay, she's kicking.
Oh.

46
00:02:22,392 --> 00:02:25,437
She's growing inside you.

47
00:02:25,479 --> 00:02:26,647
Whoa! Ooh.
Oh!

48
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:28,189
Wow, that was a big one.

49
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:31,401
I think that's
the youngest girl
ever to reject me.

50
00:02:31,443 --> 00:02:32,861
Oh, hey,
you guys.

51
00:02:32,903 --> 00:02:34,029
Oh, hey, there.
Hi.

52
00:02:34,071 --> 00:02:35,823
Hey, listen,
let me ask you.

53
00:02:35,864 --> 00:02:37,825
Do you believe
in soul mates?

54
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:38,867
Oh, yes, I do.

55
00:02:38,909 --> 00:02:40,327
I do. I believe that there

56
00:02:40,368 --> 00:02:42,203
is one perfect person out there
for everyone.

57
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:43,622
And you know how you find him?

58
00:02:43,664 --> 00:02:45,165
You stop looking for him.

59
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:48,043
That's why I've stopped looking
for Russell Crowe.

60
00:02:48,085 --> 00:02:50,337
He'll find me.

61
00:02:50,378 --> 00:02:51,672
Uh-huh, uh-huh.
And you?

62
00:02:51,713 --> 00:02:53,090
No. I mean, I believe that, uh

63
00:02:53,132 --> 00:02:55,258
certain people are more suited
for each other

64
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:56,844
and I believe in falling in love

65
00:02:56,885 --> 00:02:58,804
but soul mates--
I don't think they exist.

66
00:02:58,846 --> 00:03:00,014
Okay, good.

67
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:01,222
Why?

68
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:02,975
Well, last night,
I met Monica's.

69
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:04,852
( gasps )

70
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:08,438
What?

71
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:10,607
Yeah. I-I had a date
with this guy

72
00:03:10,649 --> 00:03:13,234
and I swear to God
he is her other half.

73
00:03:13,276 --> 00:03:14,528
Come on,
don't be crazy.

74
00:03:14,569 --> 00:03:16,279
You don't think
there's somebody out there

75
00:03:16,321 --> 00:03:17,405
better suited for Monica

76
00:03:17,447 --> 00:03:19,366
than me, do you?

77
00:03:21,576 --> 00:03:22,786
Well, what's he like?

78
00:03:23,996 --> 00:03:25,288
Well, he's tall.
Uh-huh.

79
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,414
He has brown hair.

80
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:27,749
Of course, of course.

81
00:03:27,791 --> 00:03:29,334
A tall guy with hair similar
to mine.

82
00:03:29,376 --> 00:03:32,087
Oh, unknowable universe.

83
00:03:32,129 --> 00:03:33,964
He works with food.

84
00:03:34,006 --> 00:03:35,298
Oh, sure. Older?

85
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:36,842
Obviously. And he's British.

86
00:03:36,884 --> 00:03:38,010
Oh, I was just
going to ask!

87
00:03:38,052 --> 00:03:39,344
Yeah?

88
00:03:39,386 --> 00:03:42,347
And he's-he's so centered
and mature

89
00:03:42,389 --> 00:03:43,849
and confident.
Oh...

90
00:03:43,891 --> 00:03:46,351
it's so sad they never had
a chance to meet.

91
00:03:46,393 --> 00:03:48,103
Luckily the guy she settled for

92
00:03:48,145 --> 00:03:50,189
can't hear
what you're talking about.

93
00:03:50,271 --> 00:03:51,982
Oh, I'm so sorry.

94
00:03:52,024 --> 00:03:53,192
Um, and maybe I'm wrong.

95
00:03:53,232 --> 00:03:54,985
I... but, you know what?

96
00:03:55,027 --> 00:03:57,362
I'm going to go out with him
again and I'll find out more.

97
00:03:57,404 --> 00:03:59,198
You believe that this guy
is destined for somebody else

98
00:03:59,238 --> 00:04:00,866
and you're still going
to date him?

99
00:04:00,908 --> 00:04:03,994
Well, he may not be my soul mate
but a girl's got to eat.

100
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:08,248
( knocking )

101
00:04:09,290 --> 00:04:10,751
Hey.
Hey.

102
00:04:10,792 --> 00:04:12,794
I just talked to Joey
and I just...

103
00:04:12,836 --> 00:04:14,629
I wanted to see how you were.

104
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:16,631
You know what, I still...
I can't believe it.

105
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:18,800
Joey and Rachel?
I mean it...

106
00:04:18,842 --> 00:04:22,221
It's like you and me going out,
only weirder.

107
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:25,473
All right, I know you're hurting
and-and I want to be supportive

108
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:27,517
but don't say that again.

109
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:30,311
Oh, my God, what if-if they
get married?

110
00:04:30,353 --> 00:04:32,189
Then he'd be the step-father
of my child.

111
00:04:32,231 --> 00:04:33,815
Oh, honey

112
00:04:33,857 --> 00:04:36,026
I don't think that's something
you need to worry about.

113
00:04:36,068 --> 00:04:39,071
First of all, he-he's
never going to tell her
how he feels about her.

114
00:04:39,113 --> 00:04:41,656
And even if he did,
you have no idea
how she would react.

115
00:04:41,698 --> 00:04:43,825
Sure, 'cause women never
like Joey.

116
00:04:43,867 --> 00:04:45,827
You know, I think he's
a virgin.

117
00:04:45,869 --> 00:04:47,412
But Joey...

118
00:04:47,454 --> 00:04:49,873
he's not even thinking about
going after Rachel.

119
00:04:49,915 --> 00:04:51,708
He's not?
No.

120
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:54,335
All he's thinking about
is how you're taking this.

121
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:57,005
I mean, listen, it-it's
completely freaking him out.

122
00:04:57,047 --> 00:04:58,966
He's talking about moving
to Vermont.

123
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:00,801
Why?

124
00:05:00,842 --> 00:05:03,511
He says he wants to leave
the country.

125
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:09,977
He thinks you hate him.

126
00:05:10,018 --> 00:05:13,772
Hate him? I...

127
00:05:13,814 --> 00:05:16,650
No, I don't hate him.

128
00:05:18,986 --> 00:05:21,529
It's just, it's Rachel,
you know?

129
00:05:21,571 --> 00:05:25,993
Honey, I can't even imagine
how hard this must be for you.

130
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:29,204
But I don't want you
to lose Joey over it.

131
00:05:29,246 --> 00:05:33,959
Right now he just needs to know
that you're still his friend.

132
00:05:36,503 --> 00:05:37,796
Okay. Okay,
I'll talk to him.

133
00:05:37,838 --> 00:05:38,839
Okay.

134
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:41,466
And do it soon.

135
00:05:41,508 --> 00:05:43,969
He just asked me
how he could convert his dollars

136
00:05:44,011 --> 00:05:45,929
into Vermont money.

137
00:05:51,185 --> 00:05:52,102
( Phoebe chuckling )

138
00:05:52,144 --> 00:05:53,103
Oh!
Hey.

139
00:05:53,145 --> 00:05:54,104
Oh.
Hi.

140
00:05:54,146 --> 00:05:55,314
Hi.
Um...

141
00:05:55,396 --> 00:05:56,481
Chandler, Monica,
this is Don.

142
00:05:56,523 --> 00:05:57,816
Hey.
Hello.

143
00:05:57,858 --> 00:06:00,068
Nice to meet you.

144
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:01,236
Nice to meet you.

145
00:06:01,278 --> 00:06:01,778
( coughs ):
Soul mate.

146
00:06:04,281 --> 00:06:05,573
So, what have

147
00:06:05,615 --> 00:06:06,992
you guys been doing?

148
00:06:07,034 --> 00:06:08,994
Well, we just had
a terrible lunch at Adriatica.

149
00:06:09,036 --> 00:06:11,621
What is with all the sun-dried
tomatoes at that place?

150
00:06:11,663 --> 00:06:14,166
I know. What is this, 1985?

151
00:06:14,208 --> 00:06:15,583
That's exactly what I said.

152
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:16,918
Phoebe,
isn't that strange?

153
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:18,128
Not really.

154
00:06:19,129 --> 00:06:21,965
What's wrong with
sun-dried tomatoes?

155
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:26,427
On a barbecue
chicken pizza?

156
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:28,638
No?

157
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:30,389
So, Don,
wh-what other

158
00:06:30,431 --> 00:06:31,683
restaurants do you like?

159
00:06:31,725 --> 00:06:33,434
Well, Octovio,
27 and 7.

160
00:06:33,476 --> 00:06:35,687
Oh, there's this great
little place, Alessandro's.

161
00:06:35,729 --> 00:06:37,105
Oh, my God,
that's my restaurant.

162
00:06:37,147 --> 00:06:38,106
I'm the chef there.

163
00:06:38,148 --> 00:06:39,107
You're kidding me.
No.

164
00:06:39,149 --> 00:06:40,567
Y-Your food is fantastic.

165
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:42,401
Wow, I really want to talk
to you about your menu.

166
00:06:42,443 --> 00:06:44,196
I'm just going to get
some coffees first.

167
00:06:44,238 --> 00:06:45,322
Um, anyone want anything?

168
00:06:45,364 --> 00:06:46,698
Oh, I'd like a latte.

169
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:48,783
You know what, if you're going
to talk about me

170
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:49,826
I'm going to go
with you.

171
00:06:51,410 --> 00:06:53,121
What are you doing?!

172
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:54,748
Nothing.

173
00:06:54,789 --> 00:06:56,958
I swear to God, I didn't know
you guys would be here.

174
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,920
The good news is, you don't even
believe in soul mates, so...

175
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:04,091
I believe in tall, handsome
strangers who hit on my wife.

176
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:05,842
They're just talking.

177
00:07:05,884 --> 00:07:07,802
And you know what, just 'cause
I think they're soul mates

178
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:09,470
doesn't mean anything's
going to happen.

179
00:07:09,512 --> 00:07:10,471
Phoebe?
Huh?

180
00:07:10,513 --> 00:07:11,472
Good work.
Yeah?

181
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:12,933
Yeah, I mean, he's great.

182
00:07:12,974 --> 00:07:14,351
I love him.

183
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:19,356
Don't worry,
we'll find you someone else.

184
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:25,820
( knocking )

185
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:30,951
Hey.

186
00:07:30,992 --> 00:07:32,369
Hey.

187
00:07:32,411 --> 00:07:35,997
Look, I understand
if you came by to hit me.

188
00:07:36,039 --> 00:07:37,082
I deserve it.

189
00:07:37,124 --> 00:07:39,042
No, I-I don't
want to hit you.

190
00:07:39,084 --> 00:07:42,629
Oh, what then? Kick me?

191
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:44,172
No.

192
00:07:44,214 --> 00:07:47,092
Bite me?

193
00:07:47,134 --> 00:07:50,720
No. No, I don't-I don't
want to do anything to you.

194
00:07:50,762 --> 00:07:54,682
I just want to tell you that
I'm not mad at you, and...

195
00:07:54,724 --> 00:07:57,394
and that I certainly
do not hate you.

196
00:07:59,396 --> 00:08:02,065
I just came here
to say that.

197
00:08:02,107 --> 00:08:05,277
Hey, wait, Ross, Ross.

198
00:08:05,319 --> 00:08:08,863
You want-you want to come in
for a beer or something?

199
00:08:08,905 --> 00:08:11,741
I don't know.

200
00:08:11,783 --> 00:08:13,201
Yeah, sure.

201
00:08:17,789 --> 00:08:21,168
You, uh, you got
any beer?

202
00:08:23,170 --> 00:08:25,505
All-all I got is this,
uh, melon stuff

203
00:08:25,546 --> 00:08:26,589
that Rachel left.

204
00:08:26,631 --> 00:08:28,549
Okay.

205
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:39,102
Hey, look, Ross, you
need to understand
something, okay.

206
00:08:39,144 --> 00:08:42,939
I, uh...

207
00:08:42,981 --> 00:08:47,444
I am never going to act
on this Rachel thing, okay?

208
00:08:47,486 --> 00:08:49,029
I-I wouldn't want
to do anything

209
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:50,905
to jeopardize my
friendship with you.

210
00:08:52,657 --> 00:08:54,617
Thank you.

211
00:09:00,999 --> 00:09:02,459
Mmm.

212
00:09:02,501 --> 00:09:05,128
( groans )

213
00:09:06,129 --> 00:09:08,131
( groans )

214
00:09:11,176 --> 00:09:13,261
Anyway, it, uh...

215
00:09:13,303 --> 00:09:14,846
Look, it-it'll just...

216
00:09:14,888 --> 00:09:18,016
take me a while to get
over her, that's all.

217
00:09:18,058 --> 00:09:20,394
I'm not even sure
how to do that.

218
00:09:20,435 --> 00:09:23,104
I mean, I've never
been in love before

219
00:09:23,146 --> 00:09:24,314
so...

220
00:09:24,356 --> 00:09:26,691
What? You're...?
( sighs )

221
00:09:27,859 --> 00:09:29,944
You're in love with her?

222
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:31,988
Well, yeah.

223
00:09:32,030 --> 00:09:33,532
I thought you knew that.

224
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:36,284
Um, no.

225
00:09:36,326 --> 00:09:38,578
Well, hey, look,
if-if it helps

226
00:09:38,619 --> 00:09:40,830
I don't want
to feel this way.

227
00:09:40,872 --> 00:09:41,831
Honest.

228
00:09:41,873 --> 00:09:43,250
I just keep thinking

229
00:09:43,291 --> 00:09:46,169
"Aah, I'll get over
this, you know."

230
00:09:46,211 --> 00:09:50,340
But... God, it just keeps
getting harder, and I...

231
00:09:50,382 --> 00:09:54,761
I don't... I don't know what
to do, you know.

232
00:09:54,802 --> 00:09:58,557
I don't... What do I do?

233
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:07,232
I think you-you need to
tell her how you feel.

234
00:10:07,274 --> 00:10:11,528
Okay, that's the green stuff
talking.

235
00:10:11,570 --> 00:10:12,946
No, I'm serious.

236
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:15,323
You... you need to find out
where she is

237
00:10:15,365 --> 00:10:17,534
because if she's not
where you are

238
00:10:17,576 --> 00:10:20,036
then you can start
to move past this.

239
00:10:20,078 --> 00:10:21,246
But what if, uh...

240
00:10:21,288 --> 00:10:23,457
and I'm not saying
she will be...

241
00:10:23,498 --> 00:10:28,878
If-if she is where you are,
then, uh...

242
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:32,715
then my feeling weird about it
shouldn't stand in the way.

243
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:35,343
Are you sure?

244
00:10:35,385 --> 00:10:37,887
Yeah.

245
00:10:37,929 --> 00:10:40,723
Look, if-if she's going
to end up with somebody else

246
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:44,018
the truth is, she couldn't find
a better guy, so...

247
00:10:45,437 --> 00:10:47,855
Hey, thanks.

248
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:50,984
So when do you think
you're going to talk to her?

249
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:55,071
Oh, my God, I have to tell her.

250
00:10:55,113 --> 00:10:57,407
I haven't even thought about
what I would say.

251
00:10:57,449 --> 00:10:58,950
What should I say?

252
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:01,119
I'm understanding,
but let's not get carried away.

253
00:11:01,161 --> 00:11:04,498
Right, right.
Sorry, sorry.

254
00:11:04,539 --> 00:11:07,459
( sighs ):
What am I going to say?

255
00:11:09,877 --> 00:11:11,045
Oh!

256
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:12,964
Yeah, tell me about it.

257
00:11:28,021 --> 00:11:30,482
So, I've been slowly phasing out
the wine importing

258
00:11:30,524 --> 00:11:33,318
and focusing more on
the, um, cheese side of things.

259
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:34,986
Cheese, you say?

260
00:11:35,028 --> 00:11:37,780
That's some pretty
smelly work, huh, Don?

261
00:11:39,282 --> 00:11:40,283
Excuse me?

262
00:11:40,325 --> 00:11:43,328
Cheese, it's... smelly.

263
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:46,581
You must smell
a lot of the time, too.

264
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:49,750
Uh, not really.

265
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:52,253
But when it comes to cheese,
I'm one of those people

266
00:11:52,295 --> 00:11:54,005
who thinks the smellier,
the better.

267
00:11:54,047 --> 00:11:55,131
Me, too.

268
00:11:55,173 --> 00:11:56,966
Yeah, Chandler can't stand it.

269
00:11:57,008 --> 00:11:58,968
He won't even allow me to have
blue cheese in the house.

270
00:11:59,010 --> 00:12:00,220
And you're still married to him?

271
00:12:00,261 --> 00:12:01,095
( laughing )

272
00:12:03,473 --> 00:12:05,350
( feigns laughter )

273
00:12:05,392 --> 00:12:06,643
You know what
I'd love to do?

274
00:12:06,685 --> 00:12:07,810
Hmm?

275
00:12:07,852 --> 00:12:09,354
I would like
to go to France

276
00:12:09,396 --> 00:12:11,147
and eat nothing
but bread and cheese.

277
00:12:11,189 --> 00:12:12,399
Hmm!

278
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,108
No, not even bread.
Just cheese.

279
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:15,235
Hmm.

280
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:17,320
No, I want the
bread, yeah.

281
00:12:17,362 --> 00:12:18,321
And pastries.

282
00:12:18,363 --> 00:12:19,364
Mmm...

283
00:12:19,406 --> 00:12:21,700
And paté.

284
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:22,992
Oh, I'm really not high.

285
00:12:23,034 --> 00:12:24,703
It's just that
I used to be fat.

286
00:12:24,743 --> 00:12:27,664
Oh! Well, if ever you're in
the Loire Valley, let me know.

287
00:12:27,706 --> 00:12:30,124
I've got a great little villa
you could stay at.

288
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:32,419
Is it made of cheese?

289
00:12:34,504 --> 00:12:36,172
No.

290
00:12:36,214 --> 00:12:37,674
But God, a house made of cheese!

291
00:12:37,716 --> 00:12:39,008
Wouldn't that be incredible?

292
00:12:39,050 --> 00:12:39,926
I'd move in tomorrow.

293
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:41,844
Oh, come on!

294
00:12:43,597 --> 00:12:44,889
Are you listening to this?

295
00:12:44,931 --> 00:12:46,057
I'm so sorry.

296
00:12:46,099 --> 00:12:47,225
What do I do?

297
00:12:47,267 --> 00:12:48,643
I don't know.

298
00:12:48,685 --> 00:12:50,729
They both want to live
in a house of cheese.

299
00:12:50,769 --> 00:12:52,939
I don't know how you fight that.

300
00:13:00,238 --> 00:13:02,823
Okay, okay. I can do this.

301
00:13:02,865 --> 00:13:04,367
I can tell her how I feel.

302
00:13:04,409 --> 00:13:05,660
Just, uh...

303
00:13:05,702 --> 00:13:07,245
Okay, stand up straight.

304
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:09,539
Take a couple deep breaths.

305
00:13:09,581 --> 00:13:12,333
( exhaling )

306
00:13:12,375 --> 00:13:15,086
Look confident.

307
00:13:15,128 --> 00:13:16,087
Oh!

308
00:13:16,129 --> 00:13:17,088
Geez!

309
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:18,839
Oh, Joey!
Hey.

310
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:19,840
What's up?

311
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:21,593
I, uh...

312
00:13:21,635 --> 00:13:24,638
I just came by because I-I want
to talk to you about something.

313
00:13:24,679 --> 00:13:25,930
Okay. What's up?

314
00:13:25,972 --> 00:13:27,432
Here? In the hall?

315
00:13:27,474 --> 00:13:29,808
What are we, animals?

316
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:31,269
Oh, well, honey,
I'm late for a meeting

317
00:13:31,311 --> 00:13:32,937
so could you just make it quick?

318
00:13:32,979 --> 00:13:36,608
Yeah, okay, um, I just came by
to tell you that...

319
00:13:36,650 --> 00:13:40,779
I... want to have dinner
with you tonight.

320
00:13:40,819 --> 00:13:41,446
That's all.

321
00:13:41,488 --> 00:13:42,739
Sure.
Sounds great.

322
00:13:42,781 --> 00:13:43,822
Just leave me a message

323
00:13:43,864 --> 00:13:44,365
and tell me
where to meet you, okay?

324
00:13:44,407 --> 00:13:45,032
Okay... Great.

325
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,620
Okay.
That's good. Yeah.

326
00:13:48,662 --> 00:13:50,288
Okay, that gives you
a couple of hours

327
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:51,956
to prepare
what you're going to say.

328
00:13:51,998 --> 00:13:52,915
Good, yeah.

329
00:13:52,957 --> 00:13:54,125
Oh!

330
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:56,169
Don't you people
ever knock?

331
00:13:58,171 --> 00:13:59,756
I'd like to have
Don and Phoebe over.

332
00:13:59,798 --> 00:14:00,965
Wouldn't that be nice?

333
00:14:01,007 --> 00:14:02,550
Sure.
Why don't you set it up?

334
00:14:02,592 --> 00:14:04,927
I'll just be over here,
browsing through the personals.

335
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:07,388
Are you okay?

336
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:09,432
You've been acting
weird all afternoon.

337
00:14:09,474 --> 00:14:10,975
Yeah, fine, fine.

338
00:14:11,017 --> 00:14:12,644
Not perfect!

339
00:14:12,686 --> 00:14:14,479
But good enough.

340
00:14:14,521 --> 00:14:16,481
Geez, what is with you?

341
00:14:16,523 --> 00:14:17,649
I'm sorry.

342
00:14:17,691 --> 00:14:19,734
Did you say "cheese"?

343
00:14:19,776 --> 00:14:22,987
All right,
what's going on?

344
00:14:23,029 --> 00:14:25,198
Phoebe thinks that you
and Don are soul mates.

345
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:27,200
And I don't believe
in that kind of stuff

346
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:28,867
but then you two
totally get along.

347
00:14:28,909 --> 00:14:30,537
So look, I won't
stand in your way

348
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:31,996
if you want to
run off with Don

349
00:14:32,038 --> 00:14:33,456
and live in a
house of cheese.

350
00:14:33,498 --> 00:14:36,334
Chandler, you don't believe
in soul mates?

351
00:14:36,376 --> 00:14:39,920
No, but I'm sure
"to-mah-toes" does.

352
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:42,923
I don't believe
in soul mates, either.

353
00:14:42,965 --> 00:14:44,425
You don't?

354
00:14:44,467 --> 00:14:45,635
No.

355
00:14:45,677 --> 00:14:46,969
I don't think
that you and I

356
00:14:47,011 --> 00:14:48,555
were destined
to end up together.

357
00:14:48,596 --> 00:14:50,557
I think
that we fell in love

358
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:53,184
and we work hard
at our relationship.

359
00:14:53,226 --> 00:14:55,395
Some days,
we work really hard.

360
00:14:55,436 --> 00:15:00,066
So, you don't want to live
with Don in a cheese house?

361
00:15:00,107 --> 00:15:02,861
No, I've had second thoughts
about that.

362
00:15:02,901 --> 00:15:05,530
Do you realize how hard
that would be to clean?

363
00:15:05,572 --> 00:15:07,574
I love you.

364
00:15:07,615 --> 00:15:08,575
I know.

365
00:15:08,616 --> 00:15:10,076
You know what?

366
00:15:10,117 --> 00:15:12,412
I'm going to take you
out to dinner tonight.

367
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:14,455
I found this place
that makes the greatest

368
00:15:14,497 --> 00:15:16,416
mozzarella sticks
and jalapeno poppers.

369
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:20,127
No? Really?
They taste so good.

370
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:27,635
I mean, I know
Chandler was kidding

371
00:15:27,677 --> 00:15:29,929
but it happens every time
he touches my stomach.

372
00:15:29,970 --> 00:15:31,305
I mean, I'm really worried

373
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:33,057
the baby's not
going to like him.

374
00:15:34,975 --> 00:15:36,770
Are you okay?

375
00:15:36,811 --> 00:15:39,856
Well, yeah, sure.

376
00:15:39,898 --> 00:15:40,939
Uh...

377
00:15:40,981 --> 00:15:43,943
Look, the, uh,
the reason...

378
00:15:46,780 --> 00:15:48,948
Is it hot in here?

379
00:15:48,989 --> 00:15:50,199
No, not for me.

380
00:15:50,241 --> 00:15:52,410
But why don't you take off
your sweater?

381
00:15:52,452 --> 00:15:55,121
I would, but this
is a nice place

382
00:15:55,162 --> 00:15:57,415
and my T-shirt
has a picture

383
00:15:57,457 --> 00:15:59,417
of Calvin doing Hobbes.

384
00:16:00,418 --> 00:16:01,628
Oh, my God!

385
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:02,796
Really?

386
00:16:02,837 --> 00:16:04,422
Can I see it?

387
00:16:04,464 --> 00:16:06,299
Yeah, sure.
Yeah.

388
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:07,801
Huh!

389
00:16:07,842 --> 00:16:10,887
Wow, I wouldn't think Hobbes
would like that so much.

390
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:15,642
Uh...

391
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:21,272
How long have we
known each other?

392
00:16:21,314 --> 00:16:23,190
Um... seven, eight...

393
00:16:23,232 --> 00:16:24,525
eight years.

394
00:16:24,567 --> 00:16:25,652
Wow.

395
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:26,736
Uh-huh.
Long time.

396
00:16:26,778 --> 00:16:27,904
Yeah.

397
00:16:29,155 --> 00:16:30,949
But over the past
few weeks...

398
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:32,116
I...

399
00:16:32,158 --> 00:16:33,493
Okay!

400
00:16:33,534 --> 00:16:35,161
( sighs ):
Sorry about the wait

401
00:16:35,202 --> 00:16:36,955
but it is megajammed in here.

402
00:16:36,996 --> 00:16:38,997
We have
a couple specials tonight.

403
00:16:39,039 --> 00:16:40,875
Actually, uh, could
you give us a second?

404
00:16:40,917 --> 00:16:42,001
Sure. Sure.

405
00:16:42,042 --> 00:16:43,377
Second's up.

406
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:50,343
Not... that kind of table.

407
00:16:51,511 --> 00:16:52,929
( Rachel clears her throat )

408
00:16:52,971 --> 00:16:55,014
So, you were saying?

409
00:16:56,724 --> 00:16:58,810
I'm not quite sure.

410
00:16:58,852 --> 00:17:01,980
Okay, well, you had asked me
how long we knew each other

411
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:03,523
and I said eight years.

412
00:17:03,564 --> 00:17:06,233
And then the, um,
waiter came over

413
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:08,194
and cut his tip in half.

414
00:17:08,235 --> 00:17:11,447
And, um, now here we are.

415
00:17:11,489 --> 00:17:13,115
Yeah.

416
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:15,743
Here we are.

417
00:17:15,785 --> 00:17:18,496
Uh...

418
00:17:18,538 --> 00:17:20,498
I...

419
00:17:24,168 --> 00:17:27,547
I think I'm falling
in love with you.

420
00:17:29,716 --> 00:17:31,718
What?

421
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:35,889
I'm falling in
love with you.

422
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:47,149
Who you talking to?

423
00:17:47,191 --> 00:17:48,902
Oh, you're kidding.

424
00:17:48,943 --> 00:17:51,029
Oh, it's a joke.

425
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:52,572
( silverware clanging )

426
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:54,407
Oh, that's funny.
It's funny.

427
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:56,617
I don't get it.

428
00:18:00,413 --> 00:18:02,540
Oh.

429
00:18:05,251 --> 00:18:06,544
Okay.

430
00:18:06,586 --> 00:18:09,797
Um...

431
00:18:09,839 --> 00:18:12,008
Uh, wow.

432
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:17,430
Are you, um...?

433
00:18:19,599 --> 00:18:21,517
How did, um...?

434
00:18:23,061 --> 00:18:24,645
When?

435
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:28,733
Does it really matter?

436
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:33,905
Wow, wow, wow.

437
00:18:33,947 --> 00:18:36,407
Wow, it is hot in here.

438
00:18:36,449 --> 00:18:38,910
Okay, look, look,
Rach, I know this
is a lot, okay?

439
00:18:38,952 --> 00:18:40,411
You don't have
to say anything.

440
00:18:40,453 --> 00:18:42,747
You-you, uh...

441
00:18:42,789 --> 00:18:45,291
You take as much
time as you need.

442
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:55,969
Okay, you got
to say something.

443
00:18:56,010 --> 00:18:57,553
Joey, Joey...

444
00:18:57,595 --> 00:19:00,264
I love you so much.

445
00:19:00,306 --> 00:19:01,641
But I...

446
00:19:01,682 --> 00:19:03,851
But...

447
00:19:03,893 --> 00:19:04,852
Joey?

448
00:19:04,894 --> 00:19:06,312
Yeah, right.

449
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:08,439
Hey, that's, um...

450
00:19:08,481 --> 00:19:10,650
That's okay.
That's fine.

451
00:19:10,691 --> 00:19:12,110
That's, um...

452
00:19:12,150 --> 00:19:15,613
pretty much what I was
expecting, you know.

453
00:19:15,655 --> 00:19:20,200
So, uh, it's no
big deal, all right?

454
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:24,204
I think I'm going to go.

455
00:19:24,246 --> 00:19:25,247
No!
Yeah.

456
00:19:25,289 --> 00:19:26,749
No, Joey, please, don't...

457
00:19:26,791 --> 00:19:28,709
Please don't leave like this.
Now, come on.

458
00:19:28,751 --> 00:19:31,129
( sobbing ):
You cannot do this
to a pregnant woman.

459
00:19:31,169 --> 00:19:32,296
Don't start doing that.

460
00:19:32,338 --> 00:19:34,214
You can't do that, Rach

461
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:36,342
( sobbing ):
'cause then you're
going to make me do...

462
00:19:37,468 --> 00:19:40,013
And... oh, there we go!

463
00:19:42,015 --> 00:19:43,474
Can I...?

464
00:19:43,516 --> 00:19:45,518
Oh...

465
00:19:45,559 --> 00:19:48,187
Aw, Joey, honey

466
00:19:48,228 --> 00:19:50,481
I don't want...
I don't want to lose...

467
00:19:50,523 --> 00:19:53,109
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

468
00:19:53,151 --> 00:19:55,778
You can't, okay?

469
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:57,697
Ever.

470
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:59,740
I'm so sorry.

471
00:19:59,782 --> 00:20:01,283
No, no, no, Rach.

472
00:20:01,325 --> 00:20:03,369
Please, don't be sorry.

473
00:20:03,410 --> 00:20:04,954
Okay?

474
00:20:04,996 --> 00:20:07,040
Don't be sorry.

475
00:20:07,081 --> 00:20:09,167
( sniffles )

476
00:20:12,545 --> 00:20:14,047
( sighs )

477
00:20:14,088 --> 00:20:15,589
( whispers ):
It's all right.

478
00:20:15,631 --> 00:20:17,466
You know what?
I was only kidding.

479
00:20:17,508 --> 00:20:18,718
( giggles )

480
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:21,846
Yeah, that was a real good one.

481
00:20:28,895 --> 00:20:31,689
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

482
00:20:31,731 --> 00:20:32,857
Is this your table?

483
00:20:32,899 --> 00:20:33,858
Yeah.

484
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:35,151
God, you're going to be here

485
00:20:35,193 --> 00:20:36,610
all night.
I know.

486
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:40,031
I haven't even read them
the specials yet.

487
00:20:40,073 --> 00:20:41,949
What's the matter with them?

488
00:20:41,991 --> 00:20:43,492
( sighing ):
I don't know.

489
00:20:43,534 --> 00:20:45,661
I think maybe
one of them is dying.

490
00:20:48,330 --> 00:20:49,498
Man...

491
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:51,209
Hmm, I kind of hope
it's the girl.

492
00:20:52,418 --> 00:20:55,379
The guy is really cute.

